    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d392">

                <pb facs="0397" n="385" sameAs="frus:frus1940v01/pg385"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860I.00/434: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Estonia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Wiley</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tallinn</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-07-11T13:00:00+02:00">July 11, 1940—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received July 11—10:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>88. I saw the new Foreign Minister<anchor n="61" xml:id="d392-f1"/> this morning.
                    He said that the elections would take place “with the collaboration of the
                    Communist Party”. I inquired regarding the future status of Estonia. He replied
                    that personally he did not foresee immediate <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Anschluss</hi> with the Soviet Union but could express no opinion with
                    regard to the future.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wiley</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d392-f1" n="61" xml:id="d392-f1-content">
                <p>Nigol Andresen, in the Cabinet of Dr. Vares formed on June 22, 1940.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
